    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d21">

                <pb facs="0029" n="19" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg19"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34553B/110: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-16T17:00:00+01:00">March 16, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>811. For the Secretary and Matthews. I would comment, in connection with the last
                    part of London’s telegram No. 2058 to the Department,<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d21-f1"/> that it is important that the British Ambassador be
                    instructed to state in writing to Salazar not merely that his Government desires
                    that negotiations for a second airfield be conducted directly between the United
                    States and Portugal but also that they reach a speedy and successful termination
                    without recourse to the Anglo-Portuguese agreement of August 17. It should thus
                    be made clear that the British Government fully supports our desire to build and
                    operate on our own behalf the second airfield.</p>
                <p>Reference is also made to your 750, March 11, 7 p.m.<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d21-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
